comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-15T18:53:26.967Z",codex-agent,Implementation and real-repository regression evidence linked. Review remains with the orchestrator; this item stays in progress.
  "2026-10-15T18:54:04.606Z",codex-agent,Git merge-tree executes configured pm item and history drivers. Two independently added SDK comments both survive in the merged item and history tree. Replacing the item driver with a failing command yields a tracker-path conflict. Driver receipts precede Git output; the predictor parses the NUL-delimited tree record and retains every unresolved tracker path. No source history is repaired or rewritten by simulation.
  "2026-10-15T19:02:32.565Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof: replaced only predict with the pre-feature no-conflict behavior. The real three-lane same-line conflict regression failed with ERR_ASSERTION, exit 1. Restored exact function bytes. Disjoint-file and tracker-driver predictions pass in the complete suite."
  "2026-10-15T19:11:53.235Z",codex-agent,"Base-update regression passes 1/1 on real Git: after a lane fast-forwards newer base commits then edits its own file, status lists only the lane file and no inherited-base drift. Reverting only status to the recorded starting base makes this test fail with ERR_ASSERTION, exit 1. Exact source bytes restored."
  "2026-10-15T19:35:54.457Z",codex-agent,"Round 1: add lane identities to predictions and compact conflict-only status with clean pair counts; full output retains commit and tree evidence."
  "2026-10-15T19:44:00.310Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof: restoring only the previous status function makes the named-conflict regression fail, exit 1: three predictions instead of one compact conflict. Fixed function restored exactly. Regression also checks lane IDs/branches, base identity, conflicting files, clean pair count, and full SHA/tree fields."
  "2026-10-15T19:51:36.057Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 PM-linked acceptance: pm test pm-swarm-4343 --run --progress passed 2 linked command(s), 11 tests, zero failures. Full post-run snapshots unchanged: two registered worktrees, zero parallel branches, zero swarm Git configuration keys. Source, tracker and settings mutations remained inside scratch repositories."
